# Mianx.ai autonomous execution rules

- Continue all READY tasks inside the currently approved phase
  (`execution/EXECUTION-BOARD.md`). Do not stop after every file or task to
  ask "what next?" — only stop for a real secret, a destructive action, a
  production promotion, or a materially ambiguous Founder decision.
- Verify before claiming completion: run the relevant lint/build/test/manual
  check and show the result before marking a task VERIFIED.
- Keep scope platform-first. The locked order is Mianx Core → AI Runtime →
  Project Factory → Founder Workspace → 10–12 Core Runtime Agents →
  End-to-end Beta → Telepizza and Poultry later as "Powered by Mianx.ai"
  products. Do not make RestaurantOS, Telepizza, PoultryOS, or a generic
  "AI agent agency" the current product, and do not expand this roadmap.
- Never expose, log, commit, or request real secrets/API keys. Missing
  optional env vars (Supabase, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) must degrade gracefully,
  not crash the build or the app.
- Never deploy to production, change the production domain, or merge into
  `main` without explicit Founder approval.
- Read only relevant canonical documents to control token cost: prefer
  `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `execution/EXECUTION-BOARD.md`, and the specific
  `doc/` subfolder a task touches, over scanning the whole `doc/` tree.
